cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these data, please cite the article below."
title: "Causal sequential tracking of modal horizontal wavenumbers via bounded local updates"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and data package for a causal sequential tracker of modal
  horizontal wavenumbers. One differentiable finite-rate-of-innovation initialization is
  followed by bounded, sound-speed-conditioned local updates. In a 40 m synthetic waveguide
  the tracker lowers all-frame wavenumber error by a factor of 3.09 relative to framewise
  estimation; on SWellEx-96 Event S5 a local update costs 0.108 s against 102.58 s for a
  global re-estimate. The operating limit is mode-order association, not residual fit.
  Liu Lingnan and Liu Fajun contributed equally to this work; Pengyu Wang is the
  corresponding author (wangpengyu@ouc.edu.cn).
